==Restrictions==
Rarity: Only [[:Category:Special Cats|Special]] and [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]]

==Battleground==
*1 [[Li'l Lion Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Lion Cat]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*10 [[Li'l Lion Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Lion Cats]] spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Squire Rel]] spawns as the boss after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*3 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*5 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 20.67 seconds<sup>620f</sup>, delay 3.33~10.67 seconds<sup>100f~320f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Li'l Lion Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Lion Cat]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Li'l Lion Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Lion Cat]] spawns.
**30 [[Li'l Lion Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Lion Cats]] spawn, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Li'l Lion Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Lion Cats]] spawn, delay 4~8 seconds<sup>120f~240f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Like with [[Head Shaker (Insane)|Head Shaker]] and [[Lots O' Lion (Deadly)|Lots O' Lion]], the best counter to this stage are spammable high DPS units. The restriction might limit the amount of spammable high DPS units you can use, but because you can still use units like [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] or [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], it's not that problematic. Like with Lots O' Lion, the key is to preserve [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] as much as possible (since he will be your main damage source on this stage). If the player has already beaten [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]] and gotten [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Hermit Cat]], he can become a surprisingly valuable member by doing [[Wave Attack]]s that can deal great damage to the Li'l Lion Cats (if all three hits connect) as well as chipping down incoming Li'l Lion Cats with them.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman]] cats are both exceptionally good here, being extremely spammable high DPS attackers that can do a lot of damage to the lions.
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]]: Amazing anti-traitless meatshield, albeit a bit slow. Can tank several hits from the lions before dying, which is amazing for holding the front lines.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]]: Disposable waver with a powerful wave that can deal hefty damage towards stacks of Lions and those running towards the frontline.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]]: Only accessible after beating a [[Flow Like the Stream (Merciless)|fairly difficult advent stage]], BearCat's first form has insane damage against traitless, which is not something you can easily pass up on. Being an amazing anti-traitless attacker that's usable here, he can be an amazing pick if you decide to use him.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] is still as powerful and crucial as he is in [[Lots O' Lion (Deadly)|the manic counterpart]] to this stage, dealing hefty DPS towards the Lions.

